{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgodf6qjvs","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"zonoid CLI install dir and data dir collide — rm dash rf destroys overlay graph data","summary":"The @zonoid/cli installer (packages/cli/bin/zonoid.js) hard-codes INSTALL_DIR = ~/.claude/orchestrator, which is ALSO the default CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA data dir holding overlay/, sessions/, worktrees/. checkInstallDir() runs `execSync('rm -rf ' + INSTALL_DIR)` when the source files (daemon.js / mcp-graph.js / package.json) are absent there. On a machine that runs zonoid from a SEPARATE checkout (e.g. D:\\zonoid) with data defaulting to ~/.claude/orchestrator, `init` would delete all graph data for every workspace. Verified on this box: ~/.claude/orchestrator has 10 overlay + 11 sessions + 6 worktrees entries but no source files, so init would nuke it. Additional cross-platform breakage: `rm -rf` is Unix-only (fails on Windows); skills install uses bare fs.symlinkSync (EPERM without admin/Dev-mode on Windows); and the claude harness wires stale .sh hooks (need bash/jq/curl) instead of the cross-platform Node .js hooks that bin/install.js already writes. Also note: published npm @zonoid/cli is a 0.0.1 name-reservation stub, so npx does not yet install. FIX: resolveInstallDir() reuses a complete local checkout instead of cloning; never delete a directory containing live-data subdirs; delegate claude wiring to bin/install.js (one cross-platform source of truth, full hook set); symlink to junction to copy fallback for skills.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T13:25:46.658Z","vec":[-0.10814478248357773,0.054420631378889084,-0.01720939576625824,-0.02302296832203865,0.035090960562229156,-0.1105729267001152,-0.034501541405916214,0.03207262232899666,-0.03461978957056999,0.04657096788287163,0.07977395504713058,0.02427460066974163,0.04873482137918472,0.024453354999423027,0.0345088467001915,0.03979960456490517,0.03798787668347359,-0.050403960049152374,-0.026861820369958878,-0.018842507153749466,-